(Spoiler warning!)

























	That's correct.  There will always be one at the very bottom.  You 
know you're at the bottom when there aren't any more down staircases.  ;-)
You can also tell because there will be a "clear" area around the up stair-
case, and in the S-West part of this area will be a part that looks like
	........
	----....
	   |....
	   |___.
, if you will excuse my drawing.  Search there, and you will find a secret 
door.  Go through, and you'll come to a dead end.  Search again, and you'll 
find another secret door.  Go through THAT, and you'll find a pile gems, one
of which (the gray stone) is your luckstone.  Luckstones can also be found 
lying about randomly; if you see a gray stone somewhere else, kick it.  If it
moves, it's a luckstone.  If it doesn't, it's a lodestone.  

